OL,3,GNEWSAPride of Britain award for fatal
OL,4,Atrain crash GP
OL,5,
OL,6,FA GP injured in a fatal train crash
OL,7,Fsaid she feels "honoured and lucky" to
OL,8,Fhave received a Pride of Britain award.
OL,10,FDr Eleanor Prior, 41, was in the front
OL,11,Fcarriage of the London-bound service
OL,12,Fthat crashed into a stationary
OL,13,Fintercity train near Bedford in June,
OL,14,Fkilling driver Shaun Burton, 60, and
OL,15,Fleaving 162 people injured.
OL,17,FThe force of the impact threw Prior
OL,18,Fabout eight metres along the aisle, but
OL,19,Fdespite this, she went on to care for
OL,20,Fthe passengers around her and continued
OL,21,Fto triage patients when the emergency
OL,22,Fservices arrived.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
